Cavalier was amongst the strongest Titans in Medieval England and would only bond with noble, worthy, loyal men. Belonging to the [[Casterwill family]] for generations, he was used by [[Sir Lancelot]], head of one of the main branch families. As the noblest of all [[King Arthur]]'s knights, Cavalier took on aspects of his [[Seeker]], most notably his pure heart. Eventually, Lancelot hid Cavalier's Amulet in [[Paris, France]] in his [[Mausoleum of Sir Lancelot|Mausoleum]] along with his secret books and scrolls. {{source|Memory Lane}}

Both the [[Huntik Foundation]] and [[the Organization]] became aware of Cavalier's Amulet and went to the Mausoleum recover it. After overcoming many traps and obstacles, [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Dante Vale]] reached the room where Cavalier's Amulet kept along with numerous ancient Casterwill tomes. However they were ambushed by [[Rassimov]] who went and reached the Amulet. Despite summoning the Titan, the worthy Titan refused to bond with Rassimov who declared that if he could not have the power then no one would. Rassimov then used [[Darkvoid]] to callously destroy Cavalier along with the entirety of Lancelot's books and scrolls. {{Source|Memory Lane}} 

Sophie later studied Cavalier on the [[Cypherdex]] and deduced that it was no surprise that Cavalier would not bond with an evil man like Rassimov, while Dante hauntingly confirmed to [[Guggenheim]] that, without a doubt, Cavalier had been destroyed by Rassimov's devastating power. {{source|Memory Lane}}
